  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1226 AM CDT Fri Oct 2 2026\n\nSunday through Friday:\n\nA return to northwesterly winds on Sunday as high pressure sinks\ninto the northern Plains. Expecting clearing skies and highs in\nthe upper 60s. High pressure builds into the Great Lakes region\nSunday night, with lows in the upper 30s to low 40s once again.\nWith clear skies and calm winds, frost once again becomes\npossible. High pressure lingers through Monday and Monday night,\nwith light winds, mostly clear skies, highs in the 60s, and lows\naround 40 degrees. \n\nWinds become southerly again into Tuesday as high pressure\npropagates eastward and low pressure propagates across the\nnorthern Canadian Prairies into the Hudson Bay. Expect highs in\nthe upper 60s and lows in the upper 40s to around 50 degrees. A \nweak, dry front will progress southeastward through southern \nWisconsin Tuesday night into Wednesday morning, bringing light \nwesterly winds and highs in the 70s into Wednesday as high\npressure builds from the central Plains eastward into southern\nWisconsin.\n\nHigh pressure looks to linger over the area through the end of the\nweek, with multiple weak shortwaves bringing on and off shower\npotential and highs and lows consistently around 70 and 50\ndegrees, respectively.\n\nMH",
